# 14. Preliminary Performance Framework

The eventual wildlife performance framework should operate at multiple levels.

### Population

* abundance;
* survival;
* recruitment;
* reproductive success;
* demographic structure.

### Distribution

* occupied range;
* range contraction/expansion;
* connectivity;
* fragmentation.

### Habitat

* quantity;
* quality;
* connectivity;
* degradation;
* restoration.

### Threats

* invasive species;
* habitat loss;
* disease;
* mortality;
* exploitation;
* human-wildlife conflict.

### Institutional performance

* monitoring coverage;
* response time;
* funding stability;
* plan implementation;
* interagency coordination.

### Recovery

* recovery criteria achieved;
* downlisting;
* delisting;
* post-delisting stability.

No single indicator should be treated as sufficient.

